{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/soflnps/items/648259/", "pk": 648259, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/soflnps/", "pk": 131763, "shortname": "soflnps", "name": "South Florida National Park Service", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Paddling in Paradise: Ranger-Guided Kayaking on Florida Bay", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 2, "unicode": "Paddling in Paradise: Ranger-Guided Kayaking on Florida Bay", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": false, "sold_out_text": "", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 48.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": false, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 48.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": false, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 2000, "description": "", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "**Paddling in Paradise: Ranger-Guided Kayak on Florida Bay**\n\n**Where to Meet:**\nPlease meet us at the Flamingo Marina (Florida Bay side), about 60 minutes from the Ernest F. Coe Visitor Center in Homestead. \nADDRESS: 1 Flamingo Lodge Highway, Flamingo, FL 33034\n\n**When to Meet:** \nWe ask that you arrive by 8 am to take care of last-minute logistics, sign your waivers, and prepare to paddle. If you do not check-in with a ranger by 8:15 am, your place on the tour may be forfeited to other visitors. If you miss the 8:30 am safety talk, you are not permitted on the paddle.\n\n**What to Bring:**\n* Water (required)\n* Closed-toe shoes with good tread (required)\n* Snacks\n* Hat\n* Sunglasses\n* Sunscreen\n* Bug spray or bug jacket\n* Binoculars\n* Towel\n* Dry bags\n* Breathable long-sleeve shirt and long pants\n\n**Important Reminders:**\n* Prior paddling experience, water, and closed-toe shoes with strong tread are required. If rangers don’t feel you can complete the trip safely, they may ask you to remove yourself from the trip.\n* All minors (16+) must have an adult (18+) in the kayak with them.\n* Everyone will be issued life jackets and are required to wear them for the entire paddle.\n* All visitors are required to sign a waiver. Parents or legal guardians can sign for minors.\n* You may be asked to help us lift or move kayaks short distances.\n* Plan to get wet. You may want to leave valuables, such as phones or cameras, behind so they don’t get wet. A park ranger will bring a dry bag for your car keys but will not carry any other belongings for you. The park and its rangers are not responsible for any damage to your personal belongings.\n\nWe look forward to seeing you in the ‘Glades soon!", "cancellation_notes": "Please be courteous and cancel with as much advance notice as possible so we can open your spot to other visitors.\n\nWe will only cancel the trip if there is severe weather preventing us from leading a safe experience. You will receive notification via email as well as a phone call. Conditions that may result in a cancellation include thunderstorms, lightning, or high winds. The trip could also be canceled if there is not enough water to safely follow the route.", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 15, "headline": "", "short_description": null, "image_url": "", "image_cdn_url": "", "images": [{"cls": "Image", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/soflnps/items/648259/images/1568657/", "pk": 1568657, "unicode": "photo", "gallery": "carousel", "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackconte